<title>UK: Explosion at UK chemical factory at Avonmouth.</title>
<headline>Explosion at UK chemical factory at Avonmouth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Police in Bristol, western England, said on Thursday there had been a large explosion at Avonmouth in an industrial premises.</p>
<p>The BBC said the explosion occurred in a chemical factory, owned Albright &amp; Wilson. The police said a large cloud of gas was heading up the Severn estuary and people had been advised to stay indoors. They described it as a major incident.</p>
</text>
